{
  "dom_id": "step-q269812",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{3},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,-2]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"70px\" align=\"center\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n\n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 23 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
